<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Embabo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1882</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Embabo was fought on 6 June 1882 in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a> between King Menelik of Shewa and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tekle-haymanot-of-gojjam">Tekle Haymanot of Gojjam</a>, rivals for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oromo">Oromo</a> lands south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blue-nile">Abay</a>. Menelik won and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tekle-haymanot-saint">Tekle Haymanot</a>, securing the south-west for Shewa.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-embabo.jpg" alt="Battle of Embabo" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arnaldo Cipolla · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ras_Gobana_Dacche_with_cavalry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
